  "notes": "The Forgotten brute's two-handed overhead (move forgotten-brute-overhead, 56/6/64 ticks at 60 Hz), hand-keyed (mw-ju8.25) on the greybox humanoid rig. 0-0.3 s: it sinks into a crouch with the maul dragged low, shoulders hunched. 0.3-0.62 s: a slow two-handed lift, back arching, the maul rising past the head. 0.62-0.82 s: a hold at the top, leaning back with the arms past vertical (the visible commitment that is the telegraph). 0.82-0.9333 s: the slam, torso and arms snapping forward and down with the front knee driving; the hit marker is on tick 56, the move's first active tick. 0.9333-1.1 s: it stays bent over the maul, which is stuck in the ground, through the 6 active ticks; 1.1-1.6 s it heaves and straightens slowly, wide open to a punish (the long recovery); then it settles to rest by 2.1 s. Torso: spine, chest and head point up, so a positive x tilts them back; arms and legs hang down, so a positive x swings them forward.",
